  "description": "Unavailable-window statements: which a reader recognizes, which cover an absence, and how the reader shows a covered absence.",
  "notes": "Times are RFC 3339 UTC strings and compare chronologically. A statement's receipts are those on checkpoints covering it that attest a time; accepted is true when the receipt comes from a transparency service the reader accepts as independent of the responder. Only accepted receipts register a statement and give its registration time. An absence's waiting window runs from sent_at, when the requester sent the request, to closed_at, both included. A statement case expects whether a reader recognizes it (well formed, signed by the key named, registered) and its registration time. A display case expects which statements cover the absence, how the reader shows it, and per covering statement the reason class and whether it is labelled stated afterwards.",
